.TH MODBUS-SCRAPER-CTL 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.4.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-scraper-ctl \- send commands to the modbus-scraper control server
(one-shot / batch)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-scraper-ctl
.RI [ options ] " [command ...]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one command (or a batch from stdin) to modbus-scraper's JSON-lines
control server over TCP or a unix socket, prints the replies, exits. The
one-shot sibling of \fBmodbus-scraper-cli\fR(1): no session, no
completion — the scriptable surface (the exit codes, one reply per
command). With a control token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: the
client signs every command and verifies every reply (the full sha256 of
the frame, keyed by the token).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (env CTL when unset) — same flag as the scraper itself
.TP
.B command
control command, e.g. inspect, show config, set interval 5, poll now,
request reload, request restart, shutdown
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env CONTROL_TOKEN); a file:<path> value
reads the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path, \- for stdout, or none for no local file (the
forward carries the trail); the XDG state home when unset
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-forward
also forward every audit line: none, syslog, syslog:/path,
udp://host[:port] or tcp://host[:port] (the off\-box copy,
docs/AUDIT.md)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-forward\-format
the remote forward's envelope: rfc5424 (the default) or cef — the local
syslog forms keep the verbatim send
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size, 0 = off
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail


.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-scraper-ctl poll now
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-scraper-ctl show version
.IP \(bu 2
.B printf 'inspect\enpoll now\en' | modbus-scraper-ctl
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTL ", " CONTROL_TOKEN
the control target and the TCP token when the flags are unset.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every command answered \fBok\fR.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-scraper-cli (1),
.BR modbus-scraper (1)
